      "content": "Using the hardware as intended is the easiest way to avoid data sharing, as the functionality might not be fully accessible if you interfere with the sensors. However, deliberately masking or dampening specific biological signals like heart rate or stress levels is technically challenging and could damage the chair's sophisticated internal sensors. You should thoroughly review your company's IT and privacy policies to understand exactly what data is being collected and where it is being sent. If you are very concerned, you may need to request clearer data handling agreements from your employer.",
