      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Attempting to physically obscure vital sensors with clothing is unlikely to provide a reliable shield against professional-grade biometric monitoring. Specific fabrics or sitting positions might cause inaccurate readings, but they won't guarantee that data isn't transmitted in some form. A more practical first step might be to use the chair's configuration settings, if available, to disable specific \"wellness\" features. If that fails, consider limiting use to manual adjustments rather than activating all sensing modes.",
      "source": "target",
