      "content": "Using heavy blankets or compression garments is more likely to cause discomfort or false readings than to completely block the sensors from functioning. Thermal padding might affect temperature sensors, but it is unlikely to defeat the sophisticated electrical or motion sensors tracking heart rate. Given that the settings are locked down, any physical modification carries the risk of damaging the chair or being easily detected by its diagnostics. You might consider keeping records of any unusual chair behavior or data correlations as a low-risk informational defense.",
